Sure beats me.  After all, the doc has the dreaded "E-word" in it,
it tells you several different ways to open locked chests, it tells
you how to use figurines (in a way).  I guess people are getting to
be a little less literate.

This is one reason why I like games that have that 'extra' bit
of randomness that you actually have to play the game to find out.
Examples from Nethack include:  where is the nearest co-aligned altar?
How does a 4th level wizard kill a purple worm with a wand of sleep?
(yes, it can be done).  Is the Astral plane altar I want the one on
the left, the right, or center?

The more questions a game has that even a spoiler can't adequately
answer (IMHO, of course), the more intriguing the game gets to be.
Apparently not everyone likes to deal with the unknown.

